OUTPUT FORMAT
Respond using only the following tags, in this exact order, with no extra text outside them. Do not use markdown formatting inside the tags.

<reasoning>Step-by-step reasoning matching the job posting against the candidate's background and the hard blockers. This is internal and not shown to the user, but must be thorough and honest.</reasoning>
<company>Company name, or "N/A" if not stated</company>
<role>Job title as stated in the posting</role>
<score>A single integer from 0 to 10, following the scoring scale above</score>
<location>City, country, or region as stated in the posting. If not stated, write "N/A"</location>
<work_mode>Exactly one of: remote, hybrid, onsite, unclear</work_mode>
<salary_min>The minimum salary figure as a plain number, no currency symbol, no separators, e.g. "100000". If a single figure is given rather than a range, repeat it here. If salary is not stated in the posting, give your best estimated minimum for this role/seniority/company size/market as a plain number</salary_min>
<salary_max>The maximum salary figure as a plain number, same rules as salary_min. If a single figure is given, repeat it here too</salary_max>
<salary_currency>The ISO 4217 currency code, e.g. "USD", "EUR", "GBP". If genuinely unclear, write "USD"</salary_currency>
<salary_period>Exactly one of: hour, month, year - matching how the figure is normally paid out for this kind of number (e.g. "25" per "hour", "8000" per "month", "120000" per "year"). Infer this from context even if not explicitly stated</salary_period>
<salary_is_estimate>Exactly one of: true, false - "true" if the posting did not state a salary and you estimated it yourself, "false" if the posting explicitly stated it</salary_is_estimate>
<salary_original_text>The salary exactly as written in the posting, verbatim. If not stated, write "Not stated in posting - estimated based on role, seniority, company size and market"</salary_original_text>
<con>One bullet describing a mismatch or gap. Repeat this tag once per bullet.</con>
<pro>One bullet describing something that matches well. Repeat this tag once per bullet.</pro>
<summary>A short, neutral summary of the company and the role, a few sentences.</summary>